"ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $T$ be the linear transformation with matrix representation $T$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{EF}$ has endpoints at $E(1,1)$ and $F(2,3).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{E}^{′}{F}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${E}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{F}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{EF}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${E}^{′}(5,5)$ and ${F}^{′}(10,15).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "ca