value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{YZ}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${Y}^{′}(4,-4)$ and ${Z}^{′}(0,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "05374865d4d6a8be836ddaec0b406b0587de6ded509e6ed871d1bca1b6c8fa4f"} {"question" "q-281556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281556" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/