3a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{′}(18,8),$ ${R}^{′}(-8,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "189f499fd99732bc8822a37ca68683a0b9726dc38f8e1d007e1a266a07e5db54"} {"question" "q-281566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/activity-meta